    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nMini.Sessions\n\n### Description\n\nI'm trying to setup an autocmd to load a local session if it exists, and if not to open mini.starter. I have everything working except when the session does exist and is entered syntax highlighting doesn't work until i reload the buffer via `:e`. I'm new to autocmds, but I couldn't seem to find an answer to this problem. below is a chunk from my config file.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nnow(function()\r\n\trequire(\"mini.sessions\").setup()\r\n\tlocal starter = require(\"mini.starter\")\r\n\tstarter.setup({\r\n\t\tautoopen = false,\r\n\t\titems = {\r\n\t\t\tstarter.sections.sessions(),\r\n\t\t\tstarter.sections.recent_files(5, true),\r\n\t\t\tstarter.sections.recent_files(5, false),\r\n\t\t\tstarter.sections.builtin_actions(),\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t})\r\n\trequire(\"mini.icons\").setup()\r\n\trequire(\"mini.statusline\").setup()\r\n\trequire(\"mini.tabline\").setup()\r\n\r\n\tadd({\r\n\t\tsource = \"nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter\",\r\n\t\t-- Use 'master' while monitoring updates in 'main'\r\n\t\tcheckout = \"master\",\r\n\t\tmonitor = \"main\",\r\n\t\t-- Perform action after every checkout\r\n\t\thooks = {\r\n\t\t\tpost_checkout = function()\r\n\t\t\t\tvim.cmd(\"TSUpdate\")\r\n\t\t\tend,\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t})\r\n\t-- Possible to immediately execute code which depends on the added plugin\r\n\trequire(\"nvim-treesitter.configs\").setup({\r\n\t\tensure_installed = { \"lua\", \"vimdoc\", \"typescript\", \"css\", \"html\", \"astro\" },\r\n\t\thighlight = { enable = true },\r\n\t})\r\n\r\n\tvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"VimEnter\" }, {\r\n\t\tcallback = function()\r\n\t\t\tlocal cwd = vim.fn.getcwd()\r\n\t\t\tif vim.fn.filereadable(cwd .. \"/Session.vim\") == 1 then\r\n\t\t\t\tMiniSessions.read(nil, {\r\n\t\t\t\t\tforce = true,\r\n\t\t\t\t\thooks = {\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tpost = function()\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tvim.cmd(\"edit\")\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\tend,\r\n\t\t\t\t\t},\r\n\t\t\t\t})\r\n\t\t\telse\r\n\t\t\t\tMiniStarter.open()\r\n\t\t\tend\r\n\t\tend,\r\n\t})\r\nend)\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. nvim (in a directory with Session.vim)\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4432ce87-5551-4865-a04c-910cb59b4591)\r\n\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2eb72987-448b-48fd-8c33-7aea587ef85a)",
